root=Path(r'E:\ChatGPT Codex\DDHI-SmartPharmacy')
manuals={
'Installation Guide':[
('Install the server update','On the dedicated server, run DDHI-SmartPharmacy-Server-Setup-x64.exe as Administrator. For an existing instance, keep the same installation path, data folder and Windows setup account; do not uninstall or recreate the database. Keep an encrypted backup and use approved downtime. For a new empty server, click Set up server in Initial setup; database, protected credentials and Windows services are configured automatically.'),
('Enable the local network','Open Connect computers and click Enable LAN. The app selects a network adapter automatically, creates an encrypted server identity and configures narrow local-subnet firewall rules. Simple mode needs no DNS name, manual PFX certificate, certificate password or approval-ticket field. Existing users and stock remain in the same database. First-administrator creation is needed only when no application users exist.'),
('Install every client','Install DDHI-SmartPharmacy-Setup-x64.exe version 0.2.0 on every workstation. Older clients cannot use app-managed pairing. The new client searches the local network automatically. Check the connection code against the server screen, confirm it once, then sign in with the existing staff account.'),
('Automatic future connections','The client remembers the server public key and reconnects without repeating certificate setup. It can rediscover a changed server IP with the same identity on the local network. Staff still sign in; passwords are not saved. HTTPS stays encrypted and a different server key is rejected. Do not confirm a first-time pairing code that differs from the server screen.'),
('If discovery is blocked','On the server click Save connection file. Copy that small file to a client and click Open connection file, then check the code once. The file contains only the address and public server identity, not database or staff passwords or a private key. Guest Wi-Fi isolation, separate VLANs or managed network policy can still prevent traffic; a file does not bypass blocked networking.'),
('Guide and acceptance','Server Control and the client sign-in screen include Connection guide, and the client Start Menu includes the same PDF. The complete four-page guide covers the simple flow and troubleshooting. TCP 8443 and UDP 8444 are the defaults. Windows certificate trust is not changed; verify readiness in the paired app rather than bypassing browser warnings. Physical workstation, firewall, service/reboot and hospital acceptance remain pending. Live Cerebro is disabled.')],
'Administrator Guide':[
('Accounts and separation of duties','The bootstrap account is a System Administrator, which can create users but cannot dispense medicines. Clinical roles are Chief Pharmacist and Pharmacist. Catalog approval and adjustments require Pharmacy Administrator or Chief Pharmacist. Inventory Clerk can receive and transfer. Auditors can inspect permitted reports. Individual accounts and strong passwords are mandatory; never share credentials.'),
('Sessions and security','Bearer access tickets expire after 20 minutes. Tickets are held only in desktop memory. Five failed login attempts trigger account lockout for 15 minutes. HTTP is accepted only in the Development environment for isolated loopback testing. Production requires TLS and encrypted data-protection keys. Keep PostgreSQL on loopback and restrict API ingress to hospital subnets. Production executable signing requires a hospital code-signing certificate.'),
('Manual verification policy','ManualDispensingApproved defaults to absent/disabled. Only the Chief Pharmacist can record a true policy setting, with a written hospital approval reference. Every manual dispensing also requires pharmacist authorization, confirmed patient identity and a documented reason. HID keyboard input and image decoding are unverified; this build never permits a client to assert trusted physical-device provenance.'),
('Monitoring and safe upgrades','Review near-expiry, low-stock, recalls, integration outbox and reconciliation daily. Verify the audit hash chain. Before upgrade stop DDHI services, verify an encrypted backup and preserve protected configuration and keys. Review migration SQL, apply as schema owner and reapply runtime grants. The installer does not replace database files or ProgramData settings. Installer service lifecycle on Windows Server requires a clean-server acceptance test.'),
('Boundaries','Vendor REST and read-only database adapters intentionally fail closed. The maintenance worker expires reservations; it does not post Cerebro billing. Quarantine release requires a Chief Pharmacist approval reference, and recall closure requires zero affected stock. Stock reversals preserve linked immutable movements and reject repeated reversal. Full purchase-order fulfillment and vendor-specific hardware attestation require additional approved workflows. Consult release status for the complete acceptance gap list.')],
'Pharmacy User Manual':[
('Start safely','Connect to the central HTTPS server and sign in using your individual account. Confirm the correct workstation and role. Scannerless login, lookup and inventory operations are supported. If the network fails, do not dispense offline or assume an uncertain transaction failed; review reports and reconcile before resubmitting.'),
('Catalog and receiving','Authorized catalog staff create medicine identity with explicit strength, dosage form and base unit. Barcode registration requires medicine, packaging conversion and confirmation; duplicate mappings are blocked. Receiving requires supplier, location, lot, explicit expiration, quantity, conversion and unit cost. Each delivery line needs a unique reference; separate partial deliveries and batches use separate references. Expired routine receiving is blocked.'),
('Inventory and dispensing','Use FEFO availability to choose the earliest eligible batch. Record an authorized order and minimal encounter reference. Confirm patient identity, exact medicine, strength, form, quantity, batch and expiration. The server checks remaining order quantity, available unreserved stock, recalls and the approved manual verification policy. Explicit pharmacist confirmation is required. A lookup scan never changes stock or bills a patient. Dispensing is not medication administration.'),
('Transfers, returns and counts','Transfers preserve source status and produce paired ledger entries. Returned dispensed stock enters quarantine and cannot be routinely dispensed. Returns cannot exceed the original dispensed line. Authorized stock counts create immutable adjustment movements with a reason. Recall notices block affected batches without erasing historical balances. Authorized disposition reduces stock with a reason. Recall closure requires zero remaining affected stock and does not remove historical lot blocks. Chief Pharmacist quality approval is required to release quarantined stock. Receiving, count adjustments and paired transfers can be reversed once, provided sufficient unreserved stock remains; dispensing corrections use quarantined returns.'),
('Reports and uncertainty','Reports support CSV compatible with Excel and branded printing through the Windows print dialog; choose Microsoft Print to PDF if available. Expiration views include 180, 90, 60 and 30 day filters. Month-only barcode expiry is rejected until an approved hospital policy is implemented. For a timeout inspect movements, orders and reconciliation before retrying. Obtain pharmacist and IT assistance through hospital procedures; no support contact has been invented.')],
'Barcode Scanner Setup':[
('Optional and scalable','No scanner is required for startup, login, lookup or permitted inventory functions. Scanner profiles are stored centrally by workstation, with no hardcoded scanner or workstation count. Multiple HID scanners share keyboard focus and cannot be reliably distinguished by keystrokes alone.'),
('HID and Bluetooth','Configure the device as keyboard wedge, preserve ASCII group separator 29 for GS1 variable fields and configure its suffix. Scan into the barcode entry field. Do not report a device as connected merely because a profile exists. The application classifies HID keystrokes and manual entry as unverified. The hospital must approve the resulting manual dispensing workflow before use.'),
('Serial and images','COM diagnostic lists available serial ports, without claiming they are scanners. Read COM barcode captures carriage-return-terminated input at the chosen baud rate with a 15 second timeout. Test the actual scanner communication settings before acceptance. Decode barcode image supports readable image files via ZXing and records unverified image input. Vendor SDK integration is a disabled extension boundary pending vendor support.'),
('GS1 test procedure','Test valid EAN-8, EAN-13, UPC-A, GTIN-14, GS1-128 and GS1 DataMatrix. AI 01 identifies GTIN; AI 10 lot; AI 17 expiration; AI 21 serial. Verify FNC1/AIM prefix and group separator handling, invalid check digits, duplicate fields, missing optional fields and wrong lot/expiry. Batch and expiry must never be invented when absent. Internal codes use DDHI- prefix.'),
('Hardware acceptance record','For each workstation and device record model, firmware, interface, profile, suffix, GS separator output, scanned examples, unplug/reconnect behavior and operator approval. Test zero scanners, shared HID devices and multiple devices. Actual hardware testing has not been performed by the automated software tests.')],
'Cerebro Integration Guide':[
('Authorization boundary','No approved Cerebro interface contract was supplied. Live synchronization is disabled. The mock adapter tests the local integration boundary only. REST and read-only database adapter classes reject use until vendor endpoints/schema, authentication, data ownership and written hospital authorization are supplied. Never infer undocumented endpoints or modify production tables.'),
('Ownership decisions','Cerebro retains patient, authorized medication-order and billing authority. The new application maintains its own standalone stock ledger. Hospital leadership must decide whether that ledger is operational or shadow inventory, which system deducts each movement and how opening balances and returns are reconciled. Prevent double stock deduction and duplicate billing before enabling any live posting.'),
('Approved CSV contingency','Import medicine CSV only with an approval reference and exact sample header. External IDs must be unique; similar names are never merged automatically. Authorized stock snapshots can be submitted to the snapshot comparison API; discrepancies are recorded without changing central balances. Export permitted transaction reports as CSV for approved manual posting. Manually acknowledge an outbox item only after verifying an external acknowledgment reference.'),
('Transaction safety','Inventory operations require UUID idempotency keys, retained with request fingerprints and actor identity. The same key and payload return the prior result. Different payloads with the same key are rejected. A timeout does not prove failure. Unknown vendor outcomes require NeedsReconciliation and must never trigger blind financial retry. The mock adapter does not acknowledge production transactions.'),
('Before go-live','Obtain vendor documentation and sandbox credentials, approve mapping and ownership, validate retry and delayed acknowledgment scenarios, test reconciliation and duplicate prevention, and document downtime handling. No production Cerebro testing or live writes were performed in this build.')],
'Workstation Deployment Guide':[
('Universal installation','Use DDHI-SmartPharmacy-Setup-x64.exe on each of the initial four Windows 11 x64 computers. The client is self-contained and does not require Visual Studio or Codex. The installer creates a Start Menu shortcut, optionally a desktop shortcut and an uninstaller. Each installation connects to the same central API.'),
('First run','Use client version 0.2.0 on the same hospital LAN as the server. The client searches automatically. Compare its connection code with Connect computers in Server Control, confirm once, and sign in with your individual account. Later launches remember the server identity and reconnect automatically. If discovery is blocked, open the public .ddhiconnect file saved by the server and check the same code. The application registers the computer name centrally. Pairing metadata is protected per Windows user; session tokens stay in memory. A manual hostname and trusted PFX are needed only for optional Advanced TLS.'),
('Scannerless and expansion','Verify login, medicine search, receiving, stock counts, reports and authorized administrative functions without a scanner. Configure optional HID, Bluetooth HID or COM profiles afterward. Additional workstations register through the same API; there is no hardcoded four-workstation limit. Expansion capacity must be measured under representative workloads.'),
('Connectivity and interruption','The client never connects directly to PostgreSQL. No authoritative offline stock database exists. Network failures block transactions. If a response is lost after submission, review stock movements and reconciliation before resubmitting; the desktop does not persist an offline retry queue.'),
('Pilot checklist','Record Windows version, client version, hostname, API trust, role, scanner model and test results. Test simultaneous final-unit dispensing from four real computers, expired and recalled blocks, scannerless operation, session expiration, disconnect/reconnect, uninstall/reinstall and settings preservation. Physical four-workstation acceptance remains pending.')],
'Backup Recovery Guide':[
('Credentials and objectives','Hospital IT must approve recovery time, recovery point, retention, monitoring and off-server storage. RAID is not backup. Use a dedicated PostgreSQL backup role and a hospital-managed encryption passphrase of at least 16 characters. Keep the passphrase separately from encrypted backups and test recovery access.'),
('Encrypted backup','DDHI.Pharmacy.Tools backup streams pg_dump custom-format output directly into a chunked authenticated AES-256-GCM envelope. PBKDF2-SHA256 derives the encryption key with random salt and 600000 iterations. Every chunk and final terminator is authenticated; truncated or modified backups are rejected. No plaintext dump is written by this tool. A SHA-256 sidecar supports file transfer checks, and the encrypted file is authenticated before success is reported.'),
('Scheduling','deployment/Backup.ps1 accepts tool, PostgreSQL binary and approved off-server destination paths. Supply PGHOST, PGPORT, PGUSER, PGDATABASE, PGPASSWORD and DDHI_BACKUP_PASSWORD through a protected process secret-store launcher. Register-BackupTask.ps1 schedules that launcher at 02:00 by default; no production task or secret store is installed automatically. Alert on failed tasks and missing copies.'),
('Isolated restore','Create an empty isolated database with a name beginning ddhi_restore_. Set PGDATABASE to that name and run DDHI.Pharmacy.Tools restore-test with pg_restore and the encrypted backup. The tool authenticates the entire file before sending restore data. Never point restore tests at production. Compare table counts, ledger totals and audit-chain integrity, then rehearse application workflows.'),
('Disaster recovery and limitations','Stop normal clinical workflows according to the approved downtime procedure, preserve evidence and restore only under hospital authorization. Recover protected configuration, TLS material and data-protection keys with appropriate ACLs. Reconcile all transactions since the backup before resuming. Development backup/restore tests do not establish off-server storage, power-failure resilience, service recovery or clinical disaster-recovery acceptance.')]
}
